;==========================================================================
; override.cfg  --  per-car overrides for GP2Lap (pointed to by SeasonOverrides)
;==========================================================================
; Enable by setting, in gp2lap.cfg:
;     SeasonOverrides = "override.cfg"
; If that line is commented out, or this file is missing, the feature is OFF
; and the game behaves stock.
;
; Currently supported override: per-CAR car textures (liveries).
;   carNN = <path to a BMP>
;     NN   = the in-game CAR ID (1..40). The game shows the current car's
;            name (when you switch cars) and number (in the cockpit), so you
;            can confirm which ID is which driver visually.
;     BMP  = a 256 x 164, 8-bit (256-colour) Windows BMP, in the same palette
;            as the car JAM atlases (e.g. exported from GP2Edit). Paths are
;            relative to the GP2 directory; '\' or '/' both work.
;
; A car with NO entry here renders stock (its team livery + its number).
; A bad/missing/wrong-size BMP is skipped (logged) and that car stays stock.
; Lines starting with ';', '#' or '[' are ignored.
;==========================================================================

car01 = liv\01a.bmp
car02 = liv\01b.bmp
car03 = liv\02a.bmp
car04 = liv\02b.bmp
; ... add the rest of your grid the same way (car05 = liv\03a.bmp, etc.)

;==========================================================================
; cpNN  --  per-CAR cockpit colour scheme (stock is per-team)
;==========================================================================
; The in-cockpit dashboard/surround is recoloured from THREE palette-index
; "bases" that shift three ramps of the shared cockpit image:
;     base0 -> the 0x20..0x2F ramp      (16 shades)
;     base1 -> the 0x30..0x3F ramp      (16 shades)
;     base2 -> the 0x90..0xA3 ramp      (20 shades)
; Each base is a palette index (0..255), written as decimal or 0xHH hex.
;   cpNN = base0,base1,base2
;     NN = the in-game CAR ID (1..40), same numbering as the textures above.
; A car with NO cpNN entry keeps its stock per-TEAM cockpit colours.
;
; Stock per-TEAM bases, for reference (copy a team's triple as a starting
; point for that team's drivers):
;   Williams 0x10,0x90,0x10   Tyrrell  0x10,0x10,0x01   Benetton 0x7C,0x7C,0xD6
;   McLaren  0x10,0x20,0x10   Footwork 0x10,0x10,0x90   Lotus    0x01,0x10,0x01
;   Jordan   0xDA,0x20,0x90   Larrous  0x08,0x93,0x43   Minardi  0x94,0x94,0x01
;   Ligier   0x20,0x20,0x01   Ferrari  0x01,0x01,0x01   Sauber   0x92,0x01,0x92
;   Simtek   0x08,0x08,0x08   Pacific  0x20,0x20,0x20
; (Confirm against your own carset -- an edited carset may differ.)
;==========================================================================

;cp01 = 0x10,0x90,0x10
;cp02 = 0x7C,0x7C,0xD6
